-- title:
--   Open smooth locus of the resolved model off the edge points
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0 \ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackageLevel.html#L71), i.e. a proper, flat, locally finitely presented integral model $X(N_0,q) \to \operatorname{Spec}(R_q)$ over the localisation $R_q$ of $\mathbb Q$ at $q$, with normality on affine opens, an identification of its generic geometric fibre with a smooth projective curve model for the modular function field together with Galois equivariance, the pinning of the Igusa chart and the sections $\varepsilon_\infty, \varepsilon_0$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with a ring map $\rho_O \colon R_q \to O$ and with maximal ideal generated by $q$, and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$. Assume the site hypotheses $H$ ([`V3AsmLevel.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSiteLevel.html#L270)): finiteness of the node set $\mathrm{Node}$ of the geometric $q$-fibre, existence of oriented crossing charts, étale neighbourhood data, injectivity of the assignment of node points in $X_O$, closedness of each such point, and the model hypotheses over $O$; assume moreover that each $\xi_j$ lies in the open $X_0$ of the associated chart input $C$, i.e. in the complement of the finitely many node points. Write $Y$ for the glued scheme obtained from this data and $Y \to \operatorname{Spec}(O)$ for the resulting structure morphism, $\mathrm{width}\,n = C.\mathrm{thick}\,n$ for the chain widths and $\mathrm{edgePt}\,n\,d$, $d < \mathrm{width}\,n$, for the edge points. Then there is an open subscheme $W_o \subseteq Y$ whose inclusion followed by $Y \to \operatorname{Spec}(O)$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$, and such that every point $y$ of $Y$ with $y \ne \mathrm{edgePt}\,n\,d$ for all nodes $n$ and all $d < \mathrm{width}\,n$ belongs to $W_o$.
--
--   This is the smoothness half of the construction of the resolved (regular) Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over a discrete valuation ring with residue characteristic $q$: the glued scheme $Y$ is smooth of relative dimension one over the base away from the finitely many edge points of the resolved crossing chains. It is packaged as a single existence statement so that it can be fed, together with the other properties of $Y$, into [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam).
